<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / CONFIGURATION</p>
    <h1>updateconf</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Interactively process package configuration files ending in the configured
        <code>epkgnew</code> suffix under <code>/etc</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># updateconf</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="behavior">Behavior</h2>

    <p>
        The utility compares each new configuration with its current counterpart and
        displays a unified diff. It offers Update, Discard, Edit, and Keep both;
        it requires root access and uses <code>EDITOR</code>, defaulting to
        <code>vim</code>. It does not implement an automatic three-way merge.
    </p>

    <p>
        If the current file does not exist, the new file is removed. Identical files
        are also removed. Review diffs before accepting changes; the utility is
        interactive and is not an unattended merge tool.
    </p>
</section>
